{
  "$comment": [
    "The optimisation ledger's issue list. Hand-written: id, title, severity,",
    "target and the pointer to the metric. NEVER hand-written: the measured",
    "values themselves - those are read out of results/*.json at render time by",
    "scripts/bench/render-board.mjs, because typed copies drift.",
    "",
    "`metric.path` is an array of literal keys because scenario names contain",
    "dots. `volume` applies to the db stage only. `target` is in the metric's",
    "own unit; `higherIsBetter` flips the comparison for quality scores.",
    "",
    "Regenerate the board with: npm run bench:board"
  ],
  "$baselineComment": [
    "Runs that measure the UNMODIFIED tree. They are never treated as an",
    "'after', because an after column is a claim that something was fixed.",
    "`baseline-extra` belongs here: it added the four stages the original",
    "baseline predated, on the same code, and was merged into the baseline",
    "record. Once every run carries a commit hash this list becomes redundant -",
    "a run sharing the baseline's commit cannot be an after by definition."
  ],
  "baselineLabels": ["baseline", "baseline-extra"],
  "issues": [
    {
      "id": "DB-1",
      "title": "No indexes on `journal_entries`",
      "severity": "high",
      "status": "open",
      "metricLabel": "`list.page1` p95 @ 50k",
      "metric": {
        "stage": "db",
        "volume": 50000,
        "path": ["results", "list.page1", "p95"],
        "unit": "ms",
        "target": 20
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "DB-2",
